# Release-age floor, in days: npm resolves no version published more recently
# than this, so no tree here is the first to install a compromised publish.
# Set here, npm applies it wherever it resolves a version for this project: a
# local npm install or npm update, and every lockfile Renovate writes, lock file
# maintenance included, since Renovate passes npm no --before date of its own
# when this file sets min-release-age. Versions a lockfile already records
# install as recorded, so npm ci is unaffected. npm reads the key from 11.10.0
# on; earlier npm ignores it.
#
# Keep it at or below minimumReleaseAge in the shared Renovate preset
# (github>nanohype/.github). A higher value makes npm refuse a version Renovate
# has already aged and selected, and Renovate then skips that update.
#
# packages/oauth/.npmrc holds the same floor for that package's own lockfile.
min-release-age=3
